      "content": "that's okay, but i feel like the part about \"integrating the best of both\" might actually undermine the main point of the speech. the organizers' main concern is that the core identity of the town is being diluted or replaced. if i'm being totally honest, some of the members feel like these \"new influences\" aren't actually adding anything positive to the existing local culture, and they're worried that if we try to balance both, we'll just end up losing everything that makes us who we are. is it possible to write a version that focuses more on the fact that a culture has a right to protect its original character from being overwhelmed?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
